A||N||3||WhiteFieroBlur||Fiero got washed by mother nature inside and out||||1||
Z||000000||WhiteFieroBlur||05-21-2000||02:06 PM||||  You won't beleive what I did to my fiero last night. I had my windows down and it all got rained on during a storm  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">. My seat covers are soaked, they can be washed in the washing machine right?<P>  I have always wanted to get the inside of my car cleaned but I don't think this is what I had in mind. My sunroof was up and both side windows wide open. The side door panels kind of spotted with white spots. You can beleive I won't do that again. I guess it would have been better going thru a car wash with the windows down huh? that way I could have gotten my inside clean too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>  I guess it can't be worse than me parking at my job 2 days ago in a no parking shaded part and some old woman backs into my side door and leaves a big black mark on it and takes off. I got the black mark off but she scratched the door pretty bad. I don't think I'll be parking my car like that anymore.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||05-21-2000||03:03 PM||||Use a carpet steamer with the upolstery tool. Don't machine wash the covers. They'll likely fall apart.<P>take the carpet out. hose it then let it dry a few days. make sure all the backing dries completely or you'll get mold growing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||05-21-2000||08:14 PM||||I have one of those Bissell power steamers and it works great. It gets most of the water up along with the dirt. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||DJRice||05-22-2000||09:33 AM||||If you dont pull the carpet out, rust will set in, because that insulation will hold on to that water for a long time.  The carpet can be dry, and the insulation can still be wet.<P>As for the scratch, well, they do paint those lines in the parking lot for a reason.  But it was rude of the person not even to stop, then again, they may not have had any idea they hit you.||||reg||1
